{"title":"Resources for mathematics competitions","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> hosts this <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki\" title=\"AoPS Wiki\">AoPS Wiki</a> as well as many other online resources for students interested in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">mathematics competitions</a>.  Look around the AoPS Wiki.  Individual articles often have sample problems and solutions for many levels of problem solvers.  Many also have links to books, websites, and other resources relevant to the topic.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Free_Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Free Resources</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Books\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Books</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Courses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Courses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Handouts\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Handouts</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Articles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Articles</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_Generators\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem Generators</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Contest_Problem_Sources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Contest Problem Sources</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Mathematics_Websites\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Mathematics Websites</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Mathematics_Forums\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Mathematics Forums</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Paid_Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Paid Resources</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Math_Competition_Classes\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Math Competition Classes</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Contest_Problem_Books\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Contest Problem Books</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Useful_Links\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Useful Links</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Introductory_Contests\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory Contests</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#MATHCOUNTS_Videos\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">MATHCOUNTS Videos</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Intermediate_Contests\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate Contests</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Olympiads\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiads</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Posts\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Posts</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Beginner_Olympiad_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Beginner Olympiad Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Medium/Advanced_Olympiad_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Medium/Advanced Olympiad Problems</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Free_Resources\">Free Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Free Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Books\">Books</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Books\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math books\">Math books</a></i></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>LambdaMath: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.lambdamath.dev/book-methods.html\">Zero to 150: The AMC 10/12 Playbook (contains detailed concepts and problems)</a> by Pranav Ramesh.</li>\n<li>Ritvik Rustagi's <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.tmasacademy.com/books/amc-10-12\">ACE The AMC 10 and 12 book</a></li>\n<li>OmegaLearn: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.omegalearn.org/mastering-amc8\">Mastering AMC 8 (includes video lectures)</a></li>\n<li>OmegaLearn: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.omegalearn.org/mastering-amc1012\">Mastering AMC 10/12 (includes video lectures)</a></li>\n<li>OmegaLearn: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.omegalearn.org/thebookofformulas\">The Book of Formulas</a></li>\n<li>Ritvik Rustagi's <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.tmasacademy.com/books/amc-formulas\">AMC 10/12 Key Strategies and Formulas</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//numbertheoryguy.com/publications/olympiad-number-theory-book/\">Olympiad Number Theory</a> by Justin Stevens</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//drive.google.com/file/d/1sQtirXxkEfWYuGSKDZ-d7VGYkR_idebY/view\">Olympiad Combinatorics</a> by Pranav A. Sriram.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//drive.google.com/file/d/1BcJTLjQaelZ4w_70oHKyImC2I8zLfyrt/view\">Modern Olympiad Number Theory</a> by Aditya Khurmi.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Courses\">Courses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Courses\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_courses\" title=\"Math courses\">Math courses</a></i></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtube.com/playlist?list=PL1qInO9wTp3mgEn4_X2niePNxrX26OJBl&amp;si=gNXw-2R4L7fUCIXh\">Inequalities Video tutorial by little fermat</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//math.llmlab.io/courses\">AMC Course by MathLLMlab</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//math.llmlab.io/alcumus\">AMC Practice by MathLLMlab</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.omegalearn.org/classes\">AMC/MATHCOUNTS/MOEMS Courses by OmegaLearn</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//thepuzzlr.com/math-courses\">Introduction To Number Theory by thePuzzlr</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//thepuzzlr.com/courses/amc-8-bootcamp\">AMC 8 Bootcamp by thePuzzlr</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//thepuzzlr.com/courses/amc-10-crash-course\">AMC 10 Course by thePuzzlr</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//brilliant.org/courses/math-competition-fundamentals/\">Contest Math by Brilliant</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Handouts\">Handouts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Handouts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>A general list of <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c1967976h2550333\">handouts</a> (Here's <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h1578191p15903900\">another</a>)</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//competifyhub.com/resources/\">CompetifyHub Problem Sets</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/articles/files/KedlayaInequalities.pdf\">Inequalities</a> by Dr. Kiran Kedlaya</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/articles/files/MildorfInequalities.pdf\">Olympiad Inequalities</a> by Thomas J. Mildorf</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/articles/files/MildorfNT.pdf\">Olympiad Number Theory: An Abstract Perspective</a> by Thomas J. Mildorf</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/articles/files/SatoNT.pdf\">Number Theory</a> by Naoki Sato</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//s3.amazonaws.com/aops-cdn.artofproblemsolving.com/resources/articles/bary.pdf\">Barycentric Coordinates in Olympiad Geometry</a> by Max Schindler and Evan Chen</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//s3.amazonaws.com/aops-cdn.artofproblemsolving.com/resources/articles/lifting-the-exponent.pdf\">Lifting the Exponent (LTE)</a> by Amir Hossein Parvardi</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//s3.amazonaws.com/aops-cdn.artofproblemsolving.com/resources/articles/uvw.pdf\">The uvw Method</a> by Mathias Bæk Tejs Knudsen</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//s3.amazonaws.com/aops-cdn.artofproblemsolving.com/resources/articles/crt.pdf\">The Chinese Remainder Theorem</a> by Evan Chen</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/stop-making-silly-mistakes-amc\">How to Stop Making Silly Mistakes on the AMC 10/12</a> provides actionable techniques to eliminate calculation slips, counting traps, and scantron errors.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/amc-test-strategy-anxiety-troll-problems\">AMC 10/12 Test Strategy: How to Destroy Anxiety and Outsmart \"Troll\" Problems</a> outlines psychological tips for time management, solving with detachment, and dealing with deceptive early problems.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/tricky-opening-trap-problems-amc\">15 Tricky \"Curveball\" Problems on the AMC 10/12</a> is a curated list of non-standard opening time-trap problems from recent AMC competitions.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Articles\">Articles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Articles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/news/articles/pros-cons-math-competitions\">Pros and Cons of Math Competitions</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Richard_Rusczyk\" title=\"Richard Rusczyk\">Richard Rusczyk</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/news/articles/stop-making-stupid-mistakes\">Stop Making Silly Mistakes</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Richard_Rusczyk\" title=\"Richard Rusczyk\">Richard Rusczyk</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/news/articles/how-to-write-a-solution\">How to Write a Math Solution</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Richard_Rusczyk\" title=\"Richard Rusczyk\">Richard Rusczyk</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:MCrawford\" title=\"User:MCrawford\">Mathew Crawford</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//s3.amazonaws.com/aops-cdn.artofproblemsolving.com/resources/articles/Recollection.pdf\">Contest Reflections</a> by Wanlin Li</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=How_should_I_prepare%3F\" title=\"How should I prepare?\">How should I prepare?</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//thepuzzlr.com/math-kangaroo-time-management\">Math Kangaroo Time Management</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.omegalearn.org/competitionprep\">OmegaLearn competition preparation</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/amc-pacing-blueprint-75-95\">The AMC 10/12 Pacing Blueprint for the 75–95 Scorer</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/ultimate-amc-strategy-guide-aime-usamo\">The Ultimate AMC 10/12 Strategy Guide: How to Qualify for AIME and USAMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/stop-making-silly-mistakes-amc\">How to Stop Making Silly Mistakes on the AMC 10/12</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/amc-test-strategy-anxiety-troll-problems\">AMC 10/12 Test Strategy: How to Destroy Anxiety and Outsmart \"Troll\" Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/tricky-opening-trap-problems-amc\">Tricky “Opening-Trap” Problems on the AMC 10/12</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/problems-textbooks-dont-prepare-you-for\">Problems That Textbooks Do Not Prepare You For</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/parents-and-coaches-approach-amc\">How Parents and Coaches Must Approach the AMC</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/textbook-trap-illusion-of-mastery\">The Textbook Trap and the Illusion of Mastery</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/fear-of-wasting-rare-problems\">Overcoming the Fear of \"Wasting\" Rare Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//score150.com/articles/amc-10-vs-amc-12-decision\">Do I take the AMC 10 or AMC 12?</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_Generators\">Problem Generators</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem Generators\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/alcumus\">Alcumus</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Alcumus\" title=\"Alcumus\">Wiki page</a>) on <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//amctrainer.org/\">AMC Trainer</a> A comprehensive AMC 8, AMC 10, and AMC 12 preparation platform. Practice with real problems, track your progress, and achieve your target score.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//math.llmlab.io/alcumus\">AMC 8/10/12 Practice by MathLLMlab</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Contest_Problem_Sources\">Contest Problem Sources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Contest Problem Sources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=List_of_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"List of mathematics competitions\">List of mathematics competitions</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> maintains a very large database of <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">math contest problems</a>.  Many math contest websites include archives of past problems.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=South_African_Mathematics_Olympiad\" title=\"South African Mathematics Olympiad\">South African Mathematics Olympiad</a> (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.samf.ac.za/QuestionPapers.aspx\">see here</a>) includes many years of past problems with solutions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Beestar\" title=\"Beestar\">Beestar</a> Weekly Problem Solving <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.beestar.org/exam?cmd=sdesc&amp;subj=MATH\">Weekly Challenge Math</a> - Problem Solving Challenges 1st-8th Students, weekly problem solving challenges and honor roll ranking in <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.beestar.org/exercise\">all subjects</a>.</li>\n<li>Noetic Learning <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.noetic-learning.com/gifted/index.jsp\">Challenge Math</a> - Problem Solving for the Gifted Elementary Students</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//mathteamnyc.weebly.com/mathcounts.html\">MATHCOUNTS competitions and handbooks from 2000-2017</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.thethinkacademy.com/question-wiki/home\">The Think Question Wiki</a> has numerous AMC 8 and AMC 10 past contests with PDFs and full solutions.</li>\n<li>Elias Saab's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MATHCOUNTS\" title=\"MATHCOUNTS\">MATHCOUNTS</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//mathcounts.saab.org/\">Drills page</a>.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>While the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ITest\" title=\"ITest\">iTest</a> math competition was discontinued, its problems can be found <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ITest_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"ITest Problems and Solutions\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c4676421_olympiad_math_madness_geometry_problems\">Geometry Problems from Olympiad Math Madness</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c4676480_olympiad_math_madness_inequalities_problems\">Inequality Problems from Olympiad Math Madness</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c4676503_olympiad_math_madness_number_theory_problems\">Number Theory Problems from Olympiad Math Madness</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mathematics_Websites\">Mathematics Websites</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Mathematics Websites\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_websites\" title=\"Mathematics websites\">Mathematics websites</a></i></dd></dl>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Mathematics_Forums\">Mathematics Forums</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Mathematics Forums\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_forums\" title=\"Mathematics forums\">Mathematics forums</a></i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Paid_Resources\">Paid Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Paid Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Math_Competition_Classes\">Math Competition Classes</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Math Competition Classes\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> hosts classes that are popular among many of the highest performing students in the United States.  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/school/schedule\">AoPS Class Schedule</a>. See the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/School/recommendations.php\">Art of Problem Solving Course Recommendations</a> for recommendations on choosing an AoPS course.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Contest_Problem_Books\">Contest Problem Books</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Contest Problem Books\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Many math competitions sell books of past contest problems and solutions. These books can be great supplementary material for avid students of mathematics. See <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_competition_books\" title=\"Math competition books\">this article for a full list</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Useful_Links\">Useful Links</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory_Contests\">Introductory Contests</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory Contests\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h3743248_general_advice_for_introductory_contests_amc_8mathcounts\">General Advice for Introductory Contests (AMC 8/MATHCOUNTS)</a></li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"MATHCOUNTS_Videos\">MATHCOUNTS Videos</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: MATHCOUNTS Videos\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pCWz2ADLoKI\">Introduction to MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pJHh05ksX2M?si=rXU8QG8A4BsTxBGA\">Team Round Strategies</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LY9pKbLGw-k?si=YWdJyhK4SmK75bc3\">Forms of Answers</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate_Contests\">Intermediate Contests</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate Contests\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h388108\">How preparing for the AIME will help AMC 10/12 Score</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h481746\">Best AMC 10/12 and AIME prep</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3414_amc_10\">AMC 10 Problems in the Resources Section</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\">AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3415_amc_12ahsme\">AMC 12 Problems in the Resources Section</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h357602\">Using non-AIME questions to prepare for AIME (from 2010)</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5t183f5h2971222_aime_710_level_problems\">AIME 7-10 level Problems (from 2022)</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.dropbox.com/s/icds9u5yo0xypyf/AIMElist.pdf\">BOGTRO's AIME list of topics</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.markan.net/aime/syllabus.pdf\">Sean Markan's Unofficial AIME Syllabus (also contains 58 problems)</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//omegalearn.org/aime/\">Best Resources &amp; Books for AIME</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//yu-dylan.github.io/files/handouts/M2-aime.pdf\">Dylan Yu's AIME Strategies</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//drive.google.com/file/d/0B8JbOaFM5Xo_bnc2NUd0dDFLY1U/view?pref=2&amp;pli=AIME\">AIME problems until 2014 sorted by topic</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiads\">Olympiads</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiads\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Posts\">Posts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Posts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h401061\">How to Prepare for USAJMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h399023\">USAMO preparation/doing problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h396736\">Easier Olympiads for USAJMO practice</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h366383\">For the USAMO: ACoPS or Engel</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h360619\">Olympiad problems- how to prepare</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h354103\">USAMO/Olympiads Preparation: Where to start</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/c